sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant A as Conversation Orchestrator
    participant M as LLM
    participant R as MCP Runner
    participant S as STM (short-term context)
    participant L as LTM (long-term memory)

    U->>A: Question

    rect rgb(238, 245, 255)
    Note over A,L: Every turn, automatic — the orchestrator assembles (REST)
    A->>L: Read all category memories<br/>(preference · focus · context · learning — injected without search)
    L-->>A: Memory list (truncation disclosed when over budget)
    A->>S: Load current conversation
    S-->>A: Verbatim QA (+ summary) · compaction status
    opt When compaction is needed
        A->>S: Request compaction
        S->>S: Replace older turns with a summary (summarizer LLM)
        S-->>A: Summary + verbatim after the boundary
    end
    end

    A->>M: Assemble prompt and call

    rect rgb(255, 245, 235)
    Note over A,R: MCP tools — the model requests, the runner executes
    M-->>A: Tool call request
    A->>R: Execute tool {name, arguments}
    Note over R: Identity headers overwritten by the runner → no user spoofing
    opt When a compacted-away span is needed
        R->>S: Search session · read chatlog
    end
    opt When looking up past conversations
        R->>L: Search memories (current conversation excluded)
    end
    opt When recording a lasting fact
        R->>L: Remember / update (no extraction LLM · category set)
    end
    R-->>A: Tool result
    A->>M: Tool result
    end

    M-->>A: Response
    A->>U: Answer

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
    Note over A,L: Ingest — one signal. Never blocks the response
    A->>L: Ingest signal {conversation ID, agent ID}
    L-->>A: Accepted
    Note over L: Cursor +1 only — runs once per N turns or T min of inactivity
    L->>L: Fetch source chatlog → extract memories → advance cursor
    end
